@startuml session_state
!theme cyborg
!pragma layout smetana
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam backgroundColor #0b1018
skinparam defaultFontColor #e6edf7
skinparam ArrowColor #a9b8ca
skinparam state {
 FontColor #0b1018
}
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
title Session and error transitions
[*] --> Boot
Boot --> Idle : software-observable startup checks pass
Boot --> Muted : non-Wi-Fi startup check fails / Error, mute
Idle --> Listening : Start, L2_AUDIO reports started
Idle --> Portal : long press, automatically when no Wi-Fi credentials are stored,\nor after exhausted link recovery / Idle network lease, scan then open hotspot
Portal --> Idle : verified join and save (or save warning) / show result, close access point and portal server, retain station
Portal --> Idle : cancel or inactivity / notice, teardown, retain station if connected
Portal --> Listening : Start, L2_AUDIO reports started / safe setup teardown first; retain established station
Listening --> Measuring : Heart session begins / freeze context
Listening --> Muted : audio fault / mute, block every input
Listening --> Muted : manual Stop with a deferred halting fault / show error
Measuring --> Muted : audio fault / mute, invalidate, block every input
Measuring --> Muted : manual Stop with a deferred halting fault / discard result, show error
Measuring --> Idle : Stop below minimum session length / cancel, no send
Measuring --> Analysing : Stop at or above minimum session length / mute, finalize
Analysing --> Sending : valid BPM + Wi-Fi configured + delivery prerequisites (Device id, server profile image)
Analysing --> ReportingError : invalid BPM + Wi-Fi configured + delivery prerequisites (Device id, server profile image)
Analysing --> Idle : Wi-Fi unconfigured / no send and no Wi-Fi error
Analysing --> Idle : Wi-Fi configured and delivery prerequisites fail / latch delivery-not-possible fault
Sending --> Idle : server receipt
Sending --> Idle : retries exhausted or delivery deadline reached with a qualifying clock anchor / latch delivery fault
Sending --> Idle : terminal outcome (certificate verification failure or a server rejection that a retry cannot change) / latch delivery fault at once
Sending --> Idle : no qualifying clock anchor by the delivery deadline / latch server-connection fault
ReportingError --> Idle : error report received / no numeric BPM
Sending --> Listening : Start, L2_AUDIO reports started / cancel the delivery, latch delivery fault,\nor server-connection fault before the UTC end is frozen
ReportingError --> Listening : Start, L2_AUDIO reports started / cancel the report, same latches
ReportingError --> Idle : retries exhausted or delivery deadline reached with a qualifying clock anchor / latch delivery fault
ReportingError --> Idle : terminal outcome (certificate verification failure or a server rejection that a retry cannot change) / latch delivery fault at once
ReportingError --> Idle : no qualifying clock anchor by the delivery deadline / latch server-connection fault
note as ErrorIndication
  Error latch (red LED) is independent of workflow state.
  Several errors: LEDs show the highest priority, then the first latched.
  Short press acknowledges non-restart faults; no implicit retry.
  Wi-Fi recovery does not require acknowledgement.
  Acknowledgement keeps the current workflow and causes no Start.
end note
Muted --> Boot : restart [restart-required fault]
Muted --> Idle : short press [fault clears by acknowledgement]
note right of Analysing
  Start = Busy, visible activity.
  No cancellation or queued Start.
end note
note right of Sending
  Start cancels the delivery on both send paths;
  the result is lost. Start is never queued.
  Exclusive network lease; audio stopped.
end note
note bottom of Measuring
  A session context change is latched silently and listening continues;
  after the manual Stop the device halts, discards the result and requires a restart.
  The device never applies the rejected identity and invalidates a halted acquisition.
  Wi-Fi-only faults preserve functioning audio.
  Audio faults halt listening immediately.
  The error indication is latched separately from workflow;
  acknowledgement does not change an active workflow.
end note
note bottom of Muted
  Non-Wi-Fi faults halt;
  during listening only audio faults halt at once,
  other halting faults wait for the manual Stop.
  The device mutes, invalidates incomplete work and blocks Start.
  Restart-required faults cannot be cleared by short press.
end note
@enduml
